# Nothing tracked by git lives in a subdirectory, so these four ignores cover
# every byte of video the pipeline touches. Pipeline order: raw → normalized → output.

# Source footage: 37 clips, 6.8 GB. Irreplaceable, but too large for git —
# published as GitHub release assets. Fetch with ./restore_raw_clips.sh,
# which verifies every file against raw_clips.tsv.
raw/

# build.py's working files. Rebuilt from raw/ by normalize_and_join.sh.
normalized/

# All build products: master.mp4, liturgy_training.mkv, annotations.ass,
# chapters.txt, youtube_chapters.txt, boundaries.tsv, preview.*
output/

# Parked files kept off GitHub but deliberately not deleted.
junk/

.DS_Store
__pycache__/

# The reviewer letters carry a personal phone number and this repo is public,
# so the WORDS and the built PDFs stay out. The generator itself has no
# personal data in it and is worth keeping — without this exception it would
# not survive a fresh clone.
letters/*
!letters/make_letter.py
